  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(i) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>-</mo></msup></math><br />St. No. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math> so hybridisation is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> and structure is pentagonal planar.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0178_cd337582055d.png\" style=\"width: 169px; height: 147px;\" /><br />(ii) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo></math> St. No. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math><br />so hybridisation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> and structure is trigonal bipyramidal.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0178_8a730102e8fc.png\" style=\"width: 116px; height: 111px;\" /></p>"
